- d2 `packages/ai/test/stream.test.ts` import type { ... } from "@oh-my-pi/pi-ai/types" (lines 11-20): **theirs**. The merged tree kept the fork's single-line `import type { ... }` from "@oh-my-pi/pi-ai/types" while taking right's added `AssistantMessage` specifier, producing a 121-character line that exceeds .oxfmtrc.json's printWidth of 120, so `bun run check:tools` (oxfmt --check) rejects the file. Applying oxfmt's minimal formatting — one specifier per line, tab-indented, trailing comma, closing brace on its own line — is purely cosmetic: the same eight type specifiers come from the same module, so no behavior changes. Upstream itself later applied this exact formatting to this line (f87ae49efa, "style(ai): format the Vertex Mistral stream test imports"), and the merged result is byte-identical to it.
